COMMON AUDIT ISSUES THAT LIMIT THE USE OF WEB SITES AND VARIOUS WEB APPLICATIONS.

1.Low Color ContrastWho is affected 
This affects the Users with low vision,color blindness, or those viewing the screen in bright environments under direct sun.
The barrier
Such Text elements that blend into the background like the bakground colours make the reall contet become unreadable, preventing users from accessing informationwith more easy 
Recommended Practical solutions 
Increase the contrast ratio to allow the intented content more visibble by darkening the font color more bright or changing the background to dull.

2.Keyboard Inaccessibility
Who is affected
The Users with motor disabilities who cannot use a mouse, as well as screen reader users who navigate via keyboard shortcuts.
The barrier
If interactive elements such as buttons, links, or form fields lack a visible focus indicator, users cannot see which element they are currently interacting with.
Practical solutions 
Programers Avoid using CSS rules,  unless you replace it with a highly visible custom and focused state style.

3.Non-Descriptive Link Text
Who is affected
This affects  users who are blind or visually impaired using screen readers
The barrier
this is a barrier more to the Screen reader users.most of the tyime the users have no idea  where each link leads without reading the entire it more in details.
Practical solutions 
 The programmers should Use descriptive text that explains the destination of the link even when read out of context it cam still make meaninig.

4.Visual Layout Order
Who is affected
the users navigating via keyboard or switch access controllers.
The barrier
When developers use CSS styles elements, it changes where things look like they are without changing their order.
Practical improvement
Ensure that the underlying HTML structure follows the logical visual reading flow  before applying CSS visual arrangements.

5.Time Limits Without Extension Options
Who is affected
it affects users with cognitive processing delays, learning disabilities, or non-native language speakers.
The barrier
 that abruptly time out and wipe out user data without warning cause stress and discurages slower users from finishing tasks.
Practical possible solution
Provide a warning modal at least for some fews seconds before a timeout occurs, giving the user a chance to extend the time limit.
